From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UTDeck <utdeck@invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:06:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: no OpenGL video conversion for 32-bit programs

Proton's Windows Media reader (wm_reader.c) converts the video of 32-bit programs through
OpenGL in GStreamer (glupload, glcolorconvert, glvideoflip, gldeinterlace, gldownload), because
32-bit GStreamer on a PC converts I420 to RGBA slowly, and turns that off per game by Steam app
id. On UTDeck the Unix side, and so GStreamer, is always native 64-bit ARM (32-bit programs run
through WoW64), so the reason does not apply, and GStreamer's OpenGL plugin is not on the phone.
With it on, a 32-bit program could not open an ASF video at all ("failed to create glupload",
then "asfdemux0: Internal data stream error ... not-linked", RenderFile 0x80040218), as with
Ys: Memories of Celceta's logo.wmv in stage 3.3. Use GStreamer's normal conversion, as for
64-bit programs.
---
 dlls/winegstreamer/wm_reader.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/wm_reader.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/wm_reader.c
index 51f5ac1..d8d7a8b 100644
--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/wm_reader.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/wm_reader.c
@@ -1535,7 +1535,8 @@ static void free_streams(struct wm_reader *reader)
 
 static HRESULT init_stream(struct wm_reader *reader)
 {
-    BOOL enable_opengl = sizeof(void *) == 4;
+    /* UTDeck: no OpenGL conversion (see reinit_stream). */
+    BOOL enable_opengl = FALSE;
     wg_parser_t wg_parser;
     HRESULT hr;
     WORD i;
@@ -1678,7 +1679,12 @@ out_destroy_parser:
 
 static HRESULT reinit_stream(struct wm_reader *reader, bool read_compressed)
 {
-    BOOL enable_opengl = sizeof(void *) == 4 && !read_compressed;
+    /* UTDeck: Valve converts the video of 32-bit programs through OpenGL in GStreamer, because
+     * 32-bit GStreamer on a PC converts I420 to RGBA slowly. Here the Unix side, and so GStreamer,
+     * is always native 64-bit ARM (32-bit programs run through WoW64), the reason does not apply,
+     * and GStreamer's OpenGL plugin is not on the phone: with it on, a 32-bit program's ASF video
+     * did not open at all (glupload missing, the demuxer's output not linked). */
+    BOOL enable_opengl = FALSE;
     wg_parser_t wg_parser;
     HRESULT hr;
     WORD i;
